	)
	(text "Detector: Fig. 3 half-wave peak detector. D1 replaced by Q2, a diode-connected 2N3906 (E = anode, B + C = cathode),\nso its drop tracks Q1's base-emitter drop. R14 pulls Q1's emitter up from +15 V. R15 gives Q1's base current a DC path\n(a floating input lifts the reading by I_B x R15). C1 charges through R14; release ~ (R18 + R19) x C1 ~ 0.66 s.\nR17 limits LM3916 pin 5 current when the envelope exceeds the 5 V rail.\n\nPeak LED: U2 (TLV1805, push-pull) compares AUDIO_IN directly with +15 V x R20 / (R22 + R20) = 6.0 V,\ni.e. ~12 Vpp sine. The trip point tracks the +15 V rail (not RHI). C3 holds; it discharges through R21 into\nQ3's base, so the LED fades out over ~0.5 s. Positive half-cycles only (as is the bar).\n\nSupplies: +5 V (LM3916, LEDs) ~70 mA at full scale; +15 V (R14, R22/R20, U2) ~0.6 mA; -15 V (U2) ~0.2 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6a1d2f4b-77c3-4e19-8b2a-000000000067")
	)
	(text "CLIP  red"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 349.885 45.085 0)
		(effects
